@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
title Behavior - Replace account password
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
actor "Administrator" as actor
box "Frontend - Mission Control application" #E0F2FE
  participant "ReplacePasswordDialog /\nReplacePasswordForm" as page
  participant "IAccountService / AccountService" as client
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Api" #D1FADF
  participant "CurrentAccountAuthorization" as access
  participant "AccountsController" as ctrl
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
  participant "ValidationBehavior" as validation
  participant "ReplacePasswordCommandHandler" as handler
  participant "UserAccount" as entity
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  participant "IAuditEventWriter" as audit
  database "Mission Control SQL" as db
end box
== Open: the form reads its account ==
actor -> page : Choose Replace password on a row or the details page; the dialog passes own = accountId equals currentSession().accountId
page -> client : accountResource(GetAccountQuery { id }); the action stays disabled while it loads (loading)
client -> access : GET /api/accounts/{id}, with the checks and handler of Read account details
access --> client : 200 AccountDetail, 404, or a failure
alt Account read
  client --> page : Name, email and version shown; New password and Replace password enabled; own shows the sign-out warning
else Read failed: 500 or no response
  client --> page : load-failed: alert with Try again (reload()), plus the reference ID when a 500 carried one; Cancel closes; the field and Replace password stay disabled
else 404
  client --> page : Form emits notFound; the dialog closes with NotFound; the owning page increments its counter: the details page shows its not-found state with Back to accounts, and the directory shows the "Account not found" toast
end
== Submit ==
actor -> page : Enter a new password; Replace password
page -> page : Disable repeat submission; show progress
page -> client : replacePassword(ReplacePasswordCommand: id, exact password, expectedVersion from the form's accountResource)
client -> access : PUT /api/accounts/{id}/password
alt No response: the connection dropped or the request timed out
  client --> page : replacePassword() rejects with a no-response error; the password may or may not have changed
  page -> page : failed presentation with "We couldn't confirm whether the password was replaced": keep the typed password; Replace password disabled while the account is read again, so focus moves to the alert; no reference ID
  page -> page : ReplacePasswordForm emits unconfirmed (DraftState.unconfirmed until the next answered save), which the dialog relays while it stays open; the owning page increments its counter at once, so the page behind rereads
  page -> client : ReplacePasswordForm calls reload() on its accountResource once (GET /api/accounts/{id})
  alt Read answered
    client --> page : Latest account details and version
    page --> actor : Replacing again with the same password is safe and carries the reloaded version (a stale 409 on that repeat leaves out "The password wasn't replaced"); Cancel closes with no result, since the page behind already reread
  else Own password and it did change: the read answers 401 at the current generation
    client --> page : sessionInterceptor: end(Unauthorized); the form still reports unconfirmed, so sign-in opens in session-save-unknown
  end
else Response received
access -> access : L2-002 validate signature, issuer, audience, subject, expiry (zero clock skew)
access -> db : LoadAccountAccessAsync: current status, role and credential version
db --> access : Current account access
alt Missing, invalid or expired JWT; inactive or missing account; credential version changed
  access -> audit : AppendRestrictedAsync(Denied); no payload
  access --> client : 401
  client --> page : sessionInterceptor: end(Unauthorized) once for this generation; the promise rejects with its 401, so nothing was written; login opens (session-unsaved); password not replaced
else Authenticated Collaborator (profile P: no accounts.manage)
  access -> audit : AppendRestrictedAsync(Denied); no payload
  access --> client : 403
  client --> page : refreshCapabilities() (deduplicated); ReplacePasswordForm emits forbidden; the dialog closes with Forbidden and the owning page calls showStatus(AccessDenied); password not replaced
else Administrator
  access -> ctrl : Authorized request
  ctrl -> validation : Send ReplacePasswordCommand through MediatR 12.5.0
  validation -> validation : L2-004 password 12-128 characters; never trimmed
  alt Password outside the bounds
    validation --> ctrl : 400 field error; no business mutation
    ctrl --> client : Validation ProblemDetails
    client --> page : validation state: keep the entered value; focus moves to New password, which reads its field message naming the failed bound
  else Valid request
    validation -> handler : Handle ReplacePasswordCommand
    handler -> db : Load account by ID
    db --> handler : Current account or none
    alt Account missing
      handler --> ctrl : 404; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : NotFound ProblemDetails
      client --> page : Form emits notFound; the dialog closes with NotFound; the owning page increments its counter: the details page shows its not-found state with Back to accounts, and the directory shows the "Account not found" toast
    else Stored version differs from expectedVersion
      handler --> ctrl : 409 stale version; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : Conflict ProblemDetails (stale)
      client --> page : Promise rejects with the stale 409
      page -> client : ReplacePasswordForm emits outdated and calls reload() on its accountResource once (GET /api/accounts/{id}, authorized as above)
      client --> page : Latest account details and version
      page --> actor : stale state: keep the typed password; nothing sent until Replace password is chosen again
    else Current version (designated account included; L2-008 permits this)
      handler -> entity : L2-036 salted hash of the exact password; increment credentialVersion (L2-004.4)
      entity --> handler : New hash and credential version
      handler -> db : L2-039 / L2-040 AddAuditEvent(success); SaveChangesAsync updates where version matches and commits both
      alt Racing change updated the version
        db --> handler : 0 rows; roll back update and audit
        handler --> ctrl : 409 stale version, handled as above
        ctrl --> client : Conflict ProblemDetails (stale)
        client --> page : Same handling as the stale branch above
      else Commit fails unexpectedly
        db --> handler : Roll back business state and success audit
        handler --> ctrl : Generic 500 with correlation ID
        ctrl --> client : Failure; no successful-save claim
        client --> page : failed state: nothing changed, so the old password still works; keep the new one; reference ID; Replace password retries (a busy 503 is shown the same way)
      else Commit succeeds
        db --> handler : New version and credential version
        handler --> ctrl : 200 with safe account summary; never the password or hash
        ctrl --> client : Success response
        alt Caller replaced their own password (own = true)
          client --> page : Promise resolves; the form emits draftChange (clean) and replaced
          page -> page : L2-003 ReplacePasswordDialog sets RouteContext.loginNotice = signed-out and navigates to /login with replaceUrl and router state { signOut: true }; the route guard finds no dirty draft, and the /login guard lets the sign-out navigation through while the session is still held
          page -> page : Then the dialog calls SESSION_SERVICE.end(SignedOut); ApplicationShell navigates only on Expired or Unauthorized, so nothing navigates twice
          page --> actor : Login (signed-out) with no protected data; sign in with the new password
        else Another account
          client --> page : Form emits draftChange (clean) and replaced; the dialog closes with Replaced(account); the owning page increments its counter and shows the "Password replaced" toast saying that account's current sessions end
          page --> actor : That account's earlier tokens return 401 on their next request
        end
      end
    end
  end
end
end
note over ctrl, db
Unexpected failures return generic 500 plus correlation ID (L2-043).
Diagnostics exclude secrets and contact payloads; initialization never resets this password (L2-008.3).
end note
@enduml
